  (writes through the /mnt/c 9p mount are not counted in /proc io): CPU-bound, verifying fuller blocks, not disk-bound
  revised estimate: ~2.08 M blocks at 10-20 blocks/s is 1-2 days; faster wherever blocks are near-empty again.

== Zcash testnet (zebrad 6.3.0): syncing (started 08:54Z)
  node (tools/regtest/zcash-testnet-up.sh): the pinned zebrad 6.3.0 (sha256 5e74b3b0...6e63), run inside WSL:
    <repo>/vendor/regtest/zebra/zebrad -c <repo>/.sim/zcash-testnet/zebrad.toml start
    [network] network = "Testnet"  listen_addr = "127.0.0.1:18233"  initial_mainnet_peers = []  cache_dir = ~/.dmz-regtest/zcash-testnet/peers
    [state] cache_dir = ~/.dmz-regtest/zcash-testnet/state (WSL ext4)
    [rpc] listen_addr = "127.0.0.1:18242"  enable_cookie_auth = true  cookie_dir = ~/.dmz-regtest/zcash-testnet
  listening in WSL (ss -ltnp): 127.0.0.1:18242 zebrad RPC, 127.0.0.1:18233 zebrad P2P, 127.0.0.1:18232 rpcgate
  testnet check at start: getblockhash 0 = 05a60a92d99d85997cce3b87616c089f6124d7342af37106edc76126334a2c38
    (v6.3.0 test-checkpoints.txt line 0; mainnet's is 00040fe8ec8471911baa1db1266ea15dd06b4a8a5c453883c000b031973dce08),
    getblockchaininfo chain "test": passed
  Zebra 6.3.0 RPC config has no per-method setting (zebra-rpc/src/config/rpc.rs: listen_addr, indexer_listen_addr,
    parallel_cpu_threads, debug_force_finished_sync, cookie_dir, enable_cookie_auth, max_response_body_size), so
    clients use tools/regtest/rpcgate on 127.0.0.1:18232 (own cookie at <repo>/.sim/zcash-testnet/.cookie), serving
    getblockchaininfo getblockhash getaddressutxos getaddresstxids getrawtransaction sendrawtransaction gettxout:
      no cookie            HTTP 401
      getpeerinfo          -32601 "rpcgate: method "getpeerinfo" is not served (...)"   (not forwarded)
      stop                 -32601                                                       (not forwarded)
      getinfo              -32601                                                       (not forwarded)
      submitblock          -32601                                                       (not forwarded)
      batch [..]           -32600 "rpcgate: batch requests are not served"
      getblockchaininfo    {"chain":"test","blocks":0,"estimatedheight":3568918,...}
  no update check or telemetry in zebrad 6.3.0: end_of_support.rs checks heights on Mainnet only and makes no
    request; metrics, tracing endpoint, OpenTelemetry and health endpoint are None unless configured (none are)
  first log lines: peer cache 67 testnet addresses; checkpoint ranges of 400 blocks verified every 2-3 s
  samples (zcash-testnet-up.sh; height, zebrad estimatedheight, state bytes, peers):
    08:54:54         0  3568918     349636  19
    08:56:52     13600  3556607   32003299  38
    08:57:54     20400  3554314   46665591  40
    08:59:00     26800  3532846   60775575  41
    09:00:05     34000  3522125   88208221  41
    09:01:11     37600  3521581  100044908  19
    09:02:16     39200  3521556  105264783  17
    09:04:58     54000        -  0.22 GB    40   79.2 blocks/s over the last 7 min
  zebrad's estimatedheight (~3.52-3.57 M) is below the last testnet checkpoint it ships (4,238,000), so progress uses
    that checkpoint as the target's floor (ZCASH_TESTNET_TIP_FLOOR in pins.env)
  what bounds it (10 s from /proc): zebrad CPU 14% of one core, disk write 264 KiB/s: waiting on peers, not on this
    machine; the rate fell to ~25 blocks/s while peers dropped 41 -> 17 and recovered with them (40 peers, 79/s)
  estimate: ~4.18 M blocks at 25-110 blocks/s is 10 h to 2 days; Zebra's own sync_full_testnet ceiling is 72 h;
    unstable testnet peers (zebrad/tests/e2e/sync.rs) are the risk. An estimate, not a measurement.

== Zcash testnet: primary sources consulted before starting
  state size   Zebra book, System Requirements: "Zebra uses around 300 GB for cached Mainnet data" and "10 GB for
               cached Testnet data"; "Initial sync: 300 GB download" (mainnet)
  sync time    Zebra book, Running Zebra: "A first sync from genesis takes days on Mainnet." No testnet figure.
               zebrad/tests/e2e/sync.rs v6.3.0: sync_full_testnet() -> full_sync_test(Network::new_default_testnet(), ...)
               zebrad/tests/common/sync.rs v6.3.0: FINISH_FULL_SYNC_TIMEOUT = 72 * 60 * 60 s ("The maximum time to wait
               for Zebrad to synchronize up to the chain tip starting from the genesis block")
               zebrad/tests/e2e/sync.rs: "The removed testnet variants were unreliable because testnet peers and DNS
               seeders were unstable (#1222, #1791)."
  chain        last testnet checkpoint in v6.3.0 test-checkpoints.txt: 4238000; last mainnet checkpoint: 3436171
  estimate     ~1/30 of mainnet's data: a few hours to a day here is plausible, 72 h is Zebra's own ceiling, peer
               instability the main risk. An estimate, not a measurement.

