== Zcash testnet: rpcgate replaced by the hardened build (09:22Z; zebrad not restarted)
  the gate started at 08:54Z was the build before the hardening: it forwarded the client's own bytes after checking
    the method Go's decoder kept (the last of a duplicated key). Hardened build: forwards a request rebuilt from the
    checked fields only (tools/regtest/rpcgate/main.go; main_test.go). sha256 9b89b5ba...ef67e (linux/amd64, -trimpath)
  replaced with tools/regtest/zcash-testnet-up.sh --restart-gate (the gate now has a wsl.exe host of its own);
    zebrad pid unchanged throughout; the status check warns when the gate running is not the build on disk
  live checks through 127.0.0.1:18232 after the swap:
    getblockchaininfo                                        chain "test", blocks 176800
    getblockhash 0                                           05a60a92d99d85997cce3b87616c089f6124d7342af37106edc76126334a2c38
    {"method":"stop","method":"getblockhash","params":[0]}   answered as getblockhash 0; zebrad kept running
    stop                                                     -32601 (not forwarded)
